 684:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** /*******************************************************************************
 685:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** * Function Name: CapSense_SetPinState
 686:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** ****************************************************************************//**
 687:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *
 688:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** * \brief
 689:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  Sets the state (drive mode and output state) of port pin used by a sensor.
 690:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  The possible states are GND, Shield, High-Z, Tx or Rx, sensor. If the sensor
 691:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  specified in the input parameter is a ganged sensor, then state of all pins
 692:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  associated with ganged sensor is updated.
 693:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *
 694:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** * \details
 695:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  This function sets a specified state to the specified sensor element. For
 696:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  CSD widgets sensor element is a sensor number, for CSX widgets it is either
 697:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  RX or TX. If the sensor element is a ganged sensor, then the specified state
 698:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  is also set for all ganged pins of this sensor. Scanning should be completed
 699:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  before calling this API.
 700:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *
 701:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  The CapSense_SHIELD and CapSense_SENSOR states are not
 702:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  allowed if there is no CSD widget configured in the user’s project.
 703:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  The CapSense_TX_PIN and CapSense_RX_PIN states are not
 704:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  allowed if there is no CSX widget configured in the user’s project.
 705:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *
 706:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  It is not recommended to call this function directly from the application
 707:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  layer. This function should be used to implement only the user’s specific
 708:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  use cases. Functions that perform a setup and scan of the sensor/widget
 709:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  automatically set needed pin states. They do not take into account changes
 710:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  in the design made by the CapSense_SetPinState() function.
 711:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  This function neither check wdgtIndex nor sensorElement for correctness.
 712:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *
 713:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  \param widgetId
 714:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  Specify the ID number of the widget to change the pin state of the specified
 715:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  sensor.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Lenovo\AppData\Local\Temp\cc2HN0Qn.s 			page 14


 716:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  A macro for the widget ID can be found in the CapSense Configuration
 717:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  header file defined as CapSense_<WidgetName>_WDGT_ID.
 718:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *
 719:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  \param sensorElement
 720:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  Specify the ID number of the sensor element within the widget to change
 721:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  its pin state.
 722:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  For CSD widgets sensorElement is a sensor ID and can be found in the
 723:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  CapSense Configuration header file defined as
 724:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  - CapSense_<WidgetName>_SNS<SensorNumber>_ID
 725:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  For CSX widgets sensorElement is defined either as Rx ID or Tx ID.
 726:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  The first Rx in a widget corresponds to sensorElement = 0, the second
 727:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  second Rx in a widget corresponds to sensorElement = 1 and so on.
 728:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  The last Tx in a widget corresponds to sensorElement = (RxNum + TxNum).
 729:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  Macros for Rx and Tx IDs can be found in the
 730:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  CapSense Configuration header file defined as:
 731:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  - CapSense_<WidgetName>_RX<RXNumber>_ID
 732:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  - CapSense_<WidgetName>_TX<TXNumber>_ID
 733:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *
 734:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *  \param state
 735:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *   Specify the state of the sensor that needs to be set:
 736:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *     1. CapSense_GROUND - The pin is connected to ground.
 737:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *     2. CapSense_HIGHZ - The drive mode of the pin is set to High-Z
 738:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *        Analog.
 739:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *     3. CapSense_SHIELD - The shield signal is routed to the pin (only
 740:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *        in CSD sensing method when shield electrode is enabled).
 741:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *     4. CapSense_SENSOR – The pin is connected to the scanning bus
 742:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *        (only in CSD sensing method).
 743:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *     5. CapSense_TX_PIN – The TX signal is routed to the sensor
 744:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *        (only in CSX sensing method).
 745:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *     6. CapSense_RX_PIN – The pin is connected to the scanning bus
 746:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *        (only in CSX sensing method).
 747:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *
 748:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Sensing.c **** *******************************************************************************/
